# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Bohayra Mortazavi et al. (2020). Accelerating first-principles estimation of thermal conductivity by machine-learning interatomic potentials: A MTP/ShengBTE solution.
#   Computer Physics Communications. doi:10.1016/j.cpc.2020.107583  arXiv:2009.03662v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2009.03662v1 (sha256 5cd67805c15114cb...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 537 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/mortazavi2020accelerating.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: passively trained MTPs (901 or 1,009 parameters,
# MLIP package) fitted to short AIMD runs at 50-700 K, used for
# anharmonic force constants with ShengBTE: graphene with PBE, PBEsol
# and revPBE, bulk diamond, Si, InAs and BAs, and five 2D monolayers. No
# energy/force error metrics are reported; phonons and thermal
# conductivities are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
